      "writtenOn": "2026-01-26T19:12:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MSRTSS works with both legacy and dynamic render passes. Last I checked, graphite/vk doesn\u0027t use dynamic rendering yet, because the fallback to emulate MSAA-render-to-texture needs two render passes. (Unrelated to dawn, when I get the time, my plan is to make that fallback in graphite/vk use two render passes, which would effectively be limited to desktop GPUs)\n\nAs to why it doesn\u0027t work, I can\u0027t tell without debugging. RenderDoc supports VK_EXT_msrtss, you should be able to run your tests through it and check.",
      "parentUuid": "d18ad6b2_282ebacd",
      "revId": "ec1768533e2b22c0e26cabbd4a899214eb757abe",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
